troviruses in the ovine uterus: effects of neonatal age, estrous cycle, pregnancy, and progesterone</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>75</volume><fpage>11319</fpage><lpage>11327</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11689612</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030170-b020"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dunlap</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmarini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Adelson</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Spencer</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Sheep endogenous betaretroviruses (enJSRVs) and the hyaluronidase 2 (HYAL2) receptor in the ovine uterus and conceptus</article-title><source>Biol Reprod</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>279</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15788753</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030170-b021"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dunlap</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmarini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Spencer</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Ovine endogenous betaretroviruses (enJSRVs) and placental morphogenesis</article-title><source>Placenta</source><issue>Suppl A</issue><comment>S135&#x02013;140.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030170-b022"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dunlap</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmarini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Varela</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Burghardt</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayashy</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Endoge